`Var` in a `for` loop with `setTimeout` prints the same value because of hoisting. The variable `i` is hoisted to the top of the loop, so its value is the last one assigned to it when the loop finishes.

To fix this, declare `i` inside the loop and initialize it with the desired value.

```javascript
for (var i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  (function(i) {
    setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 100);
  })(i);
}
```
